# A style handed through three generic helpers before it reaches a node, in
# two test programs.
#
# **The claim is that each style a test hands on is a class of the node
# `inner` builds, in both programs.** Each helper hands on the styles its
# `Look` carries, so the compiler only finds that `outer`'s reach a node once
# it has followed `middle`'s, and `middle`'s once it has followed `inner`'s.
# `plain` writes its style where its node is, beside them. The second program
# hands its style through `//lib/sheet`'s `spaced` first, a fourth call.
#
# Schema: the repository-case manifest, cli/tests/harness/case.rs. Textproto,
# but not a Buri file: only repo/ below is a Buri repository.

doc: "a style handed through three generic helpers is a class of its node in every test program"

run {
  args: ["test", "//..."]
  exit: 0
  golden: "pass.txt"
}
